The values is a list of 1, 3, 2, 2, 5, 2, 3, and 7.
Sort values.
The distinct is an empty list of whole numbers.
The counts is an empty list of whole numbers.
For each value in values.
The size is the number of items in distinct.
If size is 0, Place value into distinct, Place 1 into counts.
If size is more than 0.
The lastspot is size minus 1.
If item lastspot of distinct is value, set item lastspot of counts to item lastspot of counts plus 1.
If item lastspot of distinct is not value, Place value into distinct, Place 1 into counts.

The best is 0.
The final is the last position of distinct.
For every spot from 0 to final minus 1.
The nextspot is spot plus 1.
If item nextspot of distinct is item spot of distinct plus 1.
The total is item spot of counts plus item nextspot of counts.
If total is more than best, set best to total.

Show best.
